00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.900
Does it bother me?

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:18.640
This mess?

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.240
Oh, it's terrible!

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:24.860
Just an awful turn of events. Obviously not just that, but...

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:30.040
But let me turn the question back to you. What do you make of it?

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:31.540
It's very dangerous.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:34.920
I'd rather not be in the same place as a murderer.

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:39.660
So you believe that murder is inherently wrong?

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:41.040
I do.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:44.220
Killing is wrong. Pretty sure of that.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:48.840
No matter what the reason, there's nothing worse than murder.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:54.360
If you'd go that far, then tell me one thing.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:57.580
Why is it wrong to kill?

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:02.460
This is how I answer that question:

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:05.600
There is no reason.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.700
You need a reason to kill someone.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:16.440
You were angry, you just wanted them dead, whatever.
No murders happen without some sort of reason.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:17.880
But...

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:20.000
This is not a choice.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:24.860
The moment you even consider the idea you're a human failure.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:29.400
Killing people is wrong. Fundamentally wrong.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:31.860
No reason is necessary.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:36.540
Interesting. I suppose I can understand that line of thought.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:41.220
But in that case, the moment we know the killer, everything is over.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:45.240
And we'll know the killer as soon as Aikawa arrives.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:48.240
I don't know this Aikawa...person.

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:52.100
But I do. Isn't that enough?

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:56.740
Akari...tell him when Aikawa is arriving.

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:00.880
Three days from now. Faster than expected.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:07.900
That reminds me...you don't have an alibi
for either Ibuki or Sonoyama's murder.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:16.140
If you'll excuse me. It seems we are speaking a different language.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:17.280
Indeed.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:18.260
Teruko.

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:23.140
Escort him to his room. It is better not to be alone.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:26.340
And you'll be fine, right? Teruko.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:32.910
1st Floor, Storeroom Ext. Hall

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:51.700
Teruko, did you say something?

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:55.200
