00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:45.020
Seemed like Akane thought she was going to get killed.

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:48.180
What...do you mean?

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:50.320
That's the impression I got.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:55.620
Last night...we talked through the door.

00:18:56.180 --> 00:19:00.240
She seemed almost...resigned to her fate.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:06.540
Maybe Akane knew who the killer was.

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:12.290
So, Hikari...I had a talk with Teruko a few minutes ago.

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:17.050
And Teruko...Teruko <i>spoke</i>?

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:21.080
That surprised me, too.

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:25.120
But even more so...was what she said.

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:33.480
That's basically it.

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:34.800
Hikari...

00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:38.060
How much of this is true?

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:39.060
Um...

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:40.020
Well...

00:19:40.940 --> 00:19:42.120
You see...

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:42.940
Um...

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:46.820
Akari said something odd this morning as well.

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:50.580
"It's happening again." Implying...well...

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:54.080
Hikari...what did she mean by that?

00:19:54.620 --> 00:19:56.200
It's all true.

00:19:57.860 --> 00:20:02.220
Legally speaking, Miss Ilia is a criminal.

00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:06.720
We are well aware of that, but chose to serve her anyway.

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:09.600
This is why she won't call the police?

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:12.340
We simply serve her.

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:15.240
Nothing more than that.

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:18.420
Since we came to this island...things have happened.

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:22.480
That's how we got to know Aikawa...

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:23.700
Things?

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:26.480
What...things?

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:28.620
A case on this island?

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:34.120
Wait...a couple of days ago, didn't...

00:20:35.740 --> 00:20:36.780
Hey, Tomo.

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:38.560
What? Ii-chan.

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:45.500
Didn't you say you were interested in an old case that happened here?

00:20:45.980 --> 00:20:47.920
Or is my memory tricking me again?

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:48.920
It isn't.

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:51.160
So...you knew?

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:54.800
It's actually sort of infamous.

00:20:55.340 --> 00:20:58.760
Lots of people know, but nobody ever mentions it.

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:03.820
Nobody wants to piss off the Akagami Foundation.

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:09.020
Chee-kun actually mentioned it a few times.

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:12.440
But I figured I should keep it secret from you.

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:13.460
Why?

00:21:13.820 --> 00:21:15.700
I knew you'd react like this.

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:19.360
But if this was true...

00:21:20.060 --> 00:21:21.480
Then...what?

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:24.740
If the killer knew about this...

00:21:25.640 --> 00:21:30.200
If the killer knew Ilia had good reason not to call the cops...

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:40.680
That explained why the killer had been so bold,
so haughty, so immodest, and so convinced of success.

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:43.660
So, Hikari...

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:51.200
I've told a lie I may never be able to take back.

00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:53.060
I...

00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:57.300
A lie...a lie? Something you said wasn't true?

00:21:58.020 --> 00:21:58.780
Yes.

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:00.140
That night...

00:22:01.080 --> 00:22:04.580
I <i>was</i> talking with Ilia.

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:07.200
Until the earthquake.

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:10.200
That much is absolutely true.

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:15.440
But that night...that night Handa wasn't there.

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:18.460
So that's why.

00:22:19.280 --> 00:22:26.240
When we'd exchanged alibis at breakfast that morning,
Ilia had told us she'd been with Rei and Yayoi.

00:22:27.080 --> 00:22:33.080
She'd allowed everyone else to explain for themselves,
but when it was Yayoi's turn, she'd spoken first.

00:22:33.960 --> 00:22:38.940
I'd assumed it was simply because they
had been together, but apparently not.

00:22:40.180 --> 00:22:40.880
Why...?

00:22:41.260 --> 00:22:44.480
At the time...I didn't think it was a big deal.

00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:52.120
But...because of that Akane wound up
the only one without an alibi, and got locked up.

00:22:52.600 --> 00:22:54.360
And then she was murdered.

00:22:55.120 --> 00:23:00.640
And then last night, again, Ilia said that Handa had an alibi.

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:03.300
That they'd been together all night.

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:06.740
But how can we believe that?

00:23:06.940 --> 00:23:10.100
You think Rei's the killer, then?

00:23:13.640 --> 00:23:15.240
Yayoi...!

00:23:15.480 --> 00:23:21.240
If Rei is the killer, then Ilia would know that, right?

00:23:21.580 --> 00:23:23.500
Why would Ilia...?

00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:28.280
What if Ilia ordered the murders?

00:23:28.620 --> 00:23:30.180
I don't think so.

00:23:30.660 --> 00:23:36.140
I mean, both Kanami and Akane were her guests.

00:23:36.360 --> 00:23:39.980
Ever stop to wonder if she called them here...to kill them?

00:23:41.480 --> 00:23:44.720
Do you know why I was invited here?

00:23:44.720 --> 00:23:47.720
I mean...you're a genius.

00:23:48.700 --> 00:23:52.980
Cooking just isn't that big a deal.

00:23:53.540 --> 00:23:59.240
And do you know why Ibuki and Sonoyama were beheaded?

00:24:00.280 --> 00:24:01.640
You're drifting off...

00:24:01.640 --> 00:24:02.720
I am not.

00:24:03.320 --> 00:24:04.880
Eat what ails you.

00:24:05.420 --> 00:24:07.880
An idea you see in Chinese cooking.

00:24:08.700 --> 00:24:11.180
If your liver is weak, eat liver.

00:24:11.960 --> 00:24:13.920
If your belly is churning, eat stomach.

00:24:14.240 --> 00:24:14.920
Hang on...

00:24:16.100 --> 00:24:18.260
Yayoi, this is...

00:24:18.260 --> 00:24:20.540
Why was I invited here?

00:24:21.460 --> 00:24:31.400
Why was a cook like me вЂ“ not an artist or an academic
or a fortune teller or an engineer вЂ“ invited to this island?

00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:36.040
Given special treatment, allowed to stay as long as I liked?

00:24:36.420 --> 00:24:37.740
Just what...

00:24:38.120 --> 00:24:39.580
DOES SHE WANT ME TO DO!?

00:24:39.740 --> 00:24:41.200
There's no way!

00:24:41.800 --> 00:24:48.940
Miss Ilia would never do something
so awful...so horrible...not any more...

00:24:49.960 --> 00:24:55.540
I'm scared. So scared. Scared. I'm just scared.

00:24:56.060 --> 00:25:00.560
If I'm right, Kunagisa's in danger.

00:25:00.800 --> 00:25:07.240
God only knows how long before everything
above Kunagisa's shoulders is gone.

00:25:07.680 --> 00:25:11.060
This is no time to hang out and play detective.

00:25:11.320 --> 00:25:14.480
I came here because...Kunagisa's an engineer.

00:25:14.920 --> 00:25:20.480
Maybe she knows how to work a boat! We could steal the cruiser and...

00:25:20.820 --> 00:25:21.820
Wait.

00:25:24.660 --> 00:25:25.940
Say that again?

00:25:26.800 --> 00:25:27.320
Hunh?

00:25:27.480 --> 00:25:30.460
What you just said. Repeat it?

00:25:31.480 --> 00:25:34.080
Maybe we can steal...

00:25:34.080 --> 00:25:35.080
Not that.

00:25:35.740 --> 00:25:37.720
Maybe she can work a boat?

00:25:38.040 --> 00:25:39.920
No. Before that.

00:25:40.460 --> 00:25:41.920
I don't remember.

00:25:42.220 --> 00:25:44.220
Tomo. You remember, don't you?

00:25:46.520 --> 00:25:49.660
Everything above my shoulders will be gone.

00:25:50.560 --> 00:25:51.560
Bingo!

00:25:52.080 --> 00:25:55.440
Yes. That was it. That's what jumped out at me.

00:25:56.160 --> 00:25:59.560
This...this here...was the real key.

00:26:00.060 --> 00:26:00.660
Um...

00:26:01.040 --> 00:26:03.200
Quiet. I'm thinking.

00:26:05.080 --> 00:26:08.200
This might...be the right road. I'm sure it is.

00:26:08.900 --> 00:26:13.200
From here the way forward is easier than the maps of Kyoto or Sapporo.

00:26:13.560 --> 00:26:18.080
I have a theory and a solution. Now all I need is proof.

00:26:18.400 --> 00:26:20.900
We have all the clues.

00:26:21.520 --> 00:26:25.220
No...we already had them.

00:26:25.960 --> 00:26:31.020
The third case might not be the key, but it was a crucial clue.

00:26:31.880 --> 00:26:34.080
And now I had the key.

00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:36.980
I had it at last.

00:26:39.940 --> 00:26:43.080
Now, this really is nonsense...

00:26:44.880 --> 00:26:45.560
Here?

00:26:47.320 --> 00:26:48.120
No.

00:26:50.540 --> 00:26:51.740
Not like this.

00:26:52.720 --> 00:26:53.280
Tomo...

00:26:54.500 --> 00:26:55.360
What'd'ya think?

00:26:57.300 --> 00:27:01.120
I think and I think and it's no use!

00:27:01.760 --> 00:27:04.660
I can only think one thing!

00:27:05.680 --> 00:27:07.300
But it just...

00:27:10.280 --> 00:27:12.700
But it's gotta be.

00:27:13.160 --> 00:27:16.840
It's the only thing that makes sense!

00:27:17.420 --> 00:27:18.320
True.

00:27:20.220 --> 00:27:28.820
When only one possibility remains, no matter
how improbable it may seem, it has to be the truth.

00:27:29.640 --> 00:27:30.580
OK.

00:27:31.220 --> 00:27:32.200
Accept it.

00:27:32.720 --> 00:27:34.660
I don't like it at all...

00:27:35.280 --> 00:27:39.180
But this is reality. This is the truth.

00:27:41.100 --> 00:27:42.720
Yayoi. Hikari.

00:27:43.380 --> 00:27:45.860
We'll need your help.

00:27:51.800 --> 00:27:53.120
Time to fight back.

00:27:59.900 --> 00:28:05.370
The shape of the world I'd believed in

00:28:05.370 --> 00:28:08.790
Spun around when near you

00:28:08.950 --> 00:28:12.170
Leaning towards your right

00:28:12.170 --> 00:28:14.630
What I've got in my hands

00:28:14.630 --> 00:28:17.500
Is not a dream or nothing

00:28:17.500 --> 00:28:21.170
But there's something somewhere

00:28:21.170 --> 00:28:24.220
Throbbing in my heart

00:28:24.220 --> 00:28:27.140
If the one that you do love

00:28:27.140 --> 00:28:31.480
Agrees to put his arms around you

00:28:31.480 --> 00:28:34.230
Then what was a nebulous hope

00:28:34.230 --> 00:28:38.480
Shatters everything that kept you stable

00:28:38.480 --> 00:28:41.070
We'd once been so hollow

00:28:41.070 --> 00:28:43.910
Trapped inside that little box

00:28:43.910 --> 00:28:47.410
But now we've seen outside that box

00:28:47.410 --> 00:28:50.660
And have no idea where we are.

00:28:51.080 --> 00:28:52.500
That's all.

00:29:06.390 --> 00:29:08.890
Afterimages of our bliss

00:29:08.890 --> 00:29:11.720
Glimpses of the future

00:29:11.720 --> 00:29:15.310
A glance at something fragile

00:29:15.310 --> 00:29:20.150
Those times that we can still laugh together
